# Factorio.Modeler Core Library

## 📋 Overview

The Factorio.Modeler Core Library is the foundation of the Factorio Architect system. It provides:
- Throughput calculation engine
- Production chain simulation
- Bottleneck detection algorithms
- Canvas node management
- Recipe and machine data models

## 🏗️ Architecture

```
Factorio.Modeler/
├── Interfaces/
│   ├── IThroughputCalculator.cs
│   ├── ISimulationEngine.cs
│   ├── IBottleneckAnalyzer.cs
│   └── INodeManager.cs
├── Models/
│   ├── Node.cs
│   ├── Connection.cs
│   ├── Recipe.cs
│   ├── Machine.cs
│   └── SimulationResult.cs
├── Calculators/
│   ├── ThroughputCalculator.cs
│   └── AdvancedThroughputCalculator.cs
├── Simulation/
│   ├── SimulationEngine.cs
│   └── BottleneckAnalyzer.cs
└── Services/
    ├── DataPersistenceService.cs
    └── CircuitNetworkAnalyzer.cs
```

## 🧮 Throughput Calculator

### Implementation Details

The `ThroughputCalculator` implements the base formula:
```
Throughput = (Output_Per_Cycle / Crafting_Time) × Machine_Speed_Multiplier
```

### Key Methods

| Method | Description | Returns |
|--------|-------------|---------|
| `CalculateThroughput(Recipe, Machine)` | Calculate throughput for a recipe-machining combo | double |
| `ValidateRecipeChain(list<Recipe>)` | Validate production chain feasibility | ValidationResult |
| `GetBottlenecks(node_ids)` | Identify bottlenecks in node list | List<BottleneckInfo> |

### Validation Logic

All calculations are validated against:
- ✓ Crafting time constraints
- ✓ Machine capacity limits
- ✓ Circuit network throughput
- ✓ Belt transport constraints

## 🔍 Bottleneck Detection

### Algorithm Overview

The `BottleneckAnalyzer` uses:
1. Input-output rate comparison
2. Circuit network analysis
3. Belt capacity calculations
4. Queue build-up detection

```
bottleneck_score = sum(input_rates - output_rates) for all nodes in chain
if bottleneck_score > threshold:
    report_bottleneck(node, score, recommendations)
```

## 🗂️ Data Models

### Node Model
```csharp
public class Node {
    public string Id { get; set; }
    public NodeType Type { get; set; }
    public Position Position { get; set; }
    public List<Connection> Connections { get; set; }
    public ThroughputStats Throughput { get; set; }
}
```

### Connection Model
```csharp
public class Connection {
    public string SourceNodeId { get; set; }
    public string TargetNodeId { get; set; }
    public int ItemsPerTick { get; set; }
    public string Type { get; set; } // belt, pipe, circuit
}
```

## 🧪 Testing

### Gherkin Scenarios

#### Basic Throughput Calculation
```gherkin
Feature: Basic throughput calculation

  Scenario: Calculate circuit throughput
    Given a recipe for advanced circuit
    And a machine with 0.25 seconds crafting time
    When calculating throughput
    Then throughput should be 10 per minute

  Scenario: Validate production chain
    Given recipes for items A, B, and C
    And A uses 2 B items
    And B uses 1 C item
    When simulating the chain
    Then validation should pass

```

## 📖 Usage Example

```csharp
// Initialize the calculator
var calculator = new ThroughputCalculator(recipeRepository, machineRegistry);

// Calculate throughput
var recipe = await recipeRepository.GetById("circuit");
var machine = await machineRepository.GetById("advanced-circuit-provider");
var throughput = calculator.Calculate(recipe, machine); // Returns: 10/min

// Analyze bottlenecks
var bottlenecks = calculator.GetBottlenecks(new[] { node1, node2, node3 });
foreach (var bottleneck in bottlenecks) {
    logger.LogWarning($"Bottleneck at {bottleneck.Node}: {bottleneck.Score} items/sec");
}
```

